1
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:13,764
WHAT'S GOING ON?

2
00:00:13,764 --> 00:00:16,350
HUH? WELL, MY EYE
IS A LITTLE ITCHY.

3
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:20,437
UH... MINE, TOO. YEAH.

4
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,981
WOW, IT'S REALLY RED.

5
00:00:21,981 --> 00:00:23,941
YOU SHOULD GO SEE
MY EYE DOCTOR.

6
00:00:23,941 --> 00:00:26,986
RICHARD? I'M NOT GOING TO
GO SEE YOUR EX-BOYFRIEND.

7
00:00:26,986 --> 00:00:28,570
RICHARD--
THAT'S ALL I EVER HEAR.

8
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:29,864
RICHARD, RICHARD, RICHARD.

9
00:00:29,864 --> 00:00:31,490
SINCE WE'VE BEEN GOING OUT

10
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:33,826
I THINK I'VE MENTIONED
HIS NAME TWICE.

11
00:00:33,826 --> 00:00:35,786
OKAY, SO RICHARD, RICHARD.

12
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:38,288
IT'S NOT RICHARD, OKAY?

13
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:40,499
IT'S THIS NEW GUY,
AND HE'S REALLY GOOD.

14
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:43,168
WELL, I'M SORRY,
I'M NOT GOING TO AN EYE DOCTOR.

15
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:46,421
OH, GOD, HERE WE GO.
Chandler:
WHAT?

16
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:49,008
ANYTIME ANYTHING COMES
CLOSE TO TOUCHING HER EYE

17
00:00:49,008 --> 00:00:51,176
OR ANYONE ELSE'S,
SHE, LIKE, FREAKS OUT.

18
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:52,720
WATCH. WATCH.

19
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,889
ROSS! COME ON. THAT'S...
ALL RIGHT, FINE, OKAY

20
00:00:54,889 --> 00:00:56,473
I HAVE A WEIRD THING
WITH MY EYE.

21
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:58,266
CAN WE JUST NOT TALK
ABOUT IT, PLEASE?

22
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:00,686
All:
ALL RIGHT.

23
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:02,646
HEY, RACHE, YOU KNOW
THAT GREAT SONG

24
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:04,272
UM, "ME, MYSELF AND... EYE"?

25
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:06,483
AAH! MONICA! COME ON.

26
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:08,193
HEY, DOES ANYONE WANT
TO GET SOME LUNCH?

27
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,570
ALL THOSE IN FAVOR, SAY "EYE."

28
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:11,238
ROSS! STOP IT! COME ON.

29
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,907
HOW MUCH DID I LOVE

30
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:14,366
THE KING AND EYE?

31
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:15,492
CHANDLER. ALL RIGHT...

32
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,702
ME, TOO! ME, TOO! ME, TOO!

33
00:01:16,702 --> 00:01:17,912
ALL RIGHT,
JUST STOP IT!

34
00:01:17,912 --> 00:01:19,038
THAT'S ENOUGH!
COME ON.

35
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:21,415
YOU OKAY THERE, MAN?

36
00:01:21,415 --> 00:01:23,584
YEAH. I GOT TOO EXCITED.

37
00:01:30,424 --> 00:01:35,721
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

38
00:01:35,721 --> 00:01:37,973
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

39
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:40,642
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

40
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:45,564
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

41
00:01:45,564 --> 00:01:47,900
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

42
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:50,402
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

43
00:01:50,402 --> 00:01:54,322
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

44
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:56,491
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

45
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:59,202
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

46
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:00,579
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

47
00:02:00,579 --> 00:02:04,291
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

48
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:07,878
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

49
00:02:14,927 --> 00:02:16,095
ALL RIGHT,
I GOT TO GO.

50
00:02:16,095 --> 00:02:17,345
I'M TAKING BEN
TO THE PARK.

51
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:18,806
OH, GIVE HIM A KISS FOR ME.

52
00:02:18,806 --> 00:02:19,807
ALL RIGHT. BYE.

53
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:20,808
BYE.
BYE.

54
00:02:20,808 --> 00:02:21,809
LATER.

55
00:02:21,809 --> 00:02:23,351
( laughing )

56
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:25,771
I AM SO SORRY YOU GOT CAUGHT
IN THE MIDDLE OF THAT.

57
00:02:25,771 --> 00:02:29,817
I DIDN'T MEAN TO BE SO OUT THERE
BUT I AM FURIOUS WITH HIM.

58
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:33,403
WOW. UM...

59
00:02:33,403 --> 00:02:34,905
CALM DOWN?

60
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:39,367
I'M TRYING, BUT, MAN,
THAT GUY CAN PUSH MY BUTTONS.

61
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:42,287
WHY ARE YOU SO MAD AT HIM?

62
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:44,081
LOOK, I DON'T WANT
TO TALK ABOUT IT, OKAY?

63
00:02:44,081 --> 00:02:45,457
IT JUST SEEMS...

64
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:48,961
YOU WANT TO BE ON
MY LIST, TOO? KEEP TALKING.

65
00:02:48,961 --> 00:02:52,339
HAS ANYONE SEEN MY LIST,
BY THE WAY?

66
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:54,800
UH, NO, PHEEBS.
WHAT'S IT LOOK LIKE?

67
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,969
IT'S A PIECE OF PAPER,
AND IT SAYS "ROSS" ON IT.

68
00:02:56,969 --> 00:02:57,928
I SEE.

69
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:01,598
HI.
HEY.

70
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:04,518
I JUST GOT OFF THE PHONE
WITH ESTELLE, AND GUESS WHAT?

71
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:06,478
I GOT THE LEAD IN A MOVIE!

72
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:08,271
CONGRATULATIONS!
THAT'S AMAZING.

73
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:09,731
WHAT'S THE
MOVIE ABOUT?

74
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:11,483
OH, UH,
IT'S CALLED SHUTTER SPEED.

75
00:03:11,483 --> 00:03:12,901
IT'S REALLY COOL. YEAH.

76
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:14,945
UM, WELL, I MEET THIS GIRL
ON THE SUBWAY

77
00:03:14,945 --> 00:03:17,196
AND WE FALL IN LOVE
IN, LIKE, A DAY, RIGHT?

78
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:19,741
AND THEN, SHE DISAPPEARS

79
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,326
BUT I FIND OUT WHERE SHE LIVES,
AND WHEN I GET THERE

80
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:23,286
THIS, LIKE, OLD LADY
ANSWERS THE DOOR

81
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:25,039
AND I SAY, "WHERE'S BETSY?"

82
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:29,292
RIGHT? AND SHE SAYS, "BETSY'S
BEEN DEAD FOR TEN YEARS."

83
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:32,671
OOH... CHILLING.

84
00:03:32,671 --> 00:03:33,672
YEAH.

85
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:35,298
OH, AND THE BEST PART IS

86
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:37,342
WE'RE FILMING IN THE DESERT
OUTSIDE OF VEGAS.

87
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:38,927
YOU KNOW WHAT THAT
MEANS, BUDDY?

88
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:40,095
I KNOW WHAT THAT
MEANS, BUDDY.

89
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:42,056
ROAD TRIP! YEAH.
WE CAN RENT A CAR.

90
00:03:42,056 --> 00:03:44,058
I JUST HAVE TO BE THERE
BY TUESDAY.

91
00:03:44,058 --> 00:03:46,768
OOH, WAIT,
MY GRANDMOTHER'S DEAD.

92
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:54,275
WELL, UH... WE CAN TALK
ABOUT THAT, TOO, PHEEBS.

93
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:55,736
NO, NO.

94
00:03:55,736 --> 00:03:57,863
HER CAB--
SHE PROBABLY WON'T BE USING IT.

95
00:03:57,863 --> 00:03:59,614
YOU COULD DRIVE IT TO LAS VEGAS.

96
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:01,324
ALL RIGHT! THANKS, PHEEBS.

97
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,701
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA, WHOA, WHOA.

98
00:04:02,701 --> 00:04:04,411
WHAT ARE WE GOING TO DO
ABOUT MY JOB?

99
00:04:04,411 --> 00:04:05,829
OH, UH, NOT GO.

100
00:04:05,829 --> 00:04:07,622
ALL RIGHT! GREAT!
ROAD TRIP, BABY!

101
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:08,665
( chortling )

102
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,209
IS THIS OKAY WITH YOU?

103
00:04:10,209 --> 00:04:13,045
CHANDLER, YOU DON'T HAVE
TO ASK FOR MY PERMISSION.

104
00:04:13,045 --> 00:04:14,922
YOU CAN GO.
THANK YOU.

105
00:04:14,922 --> 00:04:16,715
HEY, RACHE, COME ON.

106
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,842
YOU'LL BE LATE
FOR THE EYE DOCTOR APPOINTMENT.

107
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:21,511
ALL RIGHT.
LET'S GET THIS OVER WITH.

108
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:22,804
( groans )

109
00:04:23,847 --> 00:04:26,183
OH... NO.

110
00:04:26,183 --> 00:04:29,561
LOOK WHAT I DID.

111
00:04:29,561 --> 00:04:31,396
OH...

112
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:34,274
I MEAN, LOOK AT THIS MESS.

113
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:37,402
I MEAN, WE'RE GOING TO PROBABLY
HAVE TO CLEAN THIS UP, YOU KNOW?

114
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:40,072
I MEAN, WE'RE GOING
TO HAVE TO RESCHEDULE.

115
00:04:40,072 --> 00:04:43,200
IF YOU THOUGHT THAT THIS MESS
WAS GOING TO BOTHER ME

116
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:44,868
YOU ARE WRONG.

117
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:47,037
ALL RIGHT,
LET'S GO, BLINKY.
ALL RIGHT.

118
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:49,164
( Rachel groans in frustration)

119
00:04:51,125 --> 00:04:52,500
CHANDLER...

120
00:04:57,881 --> 00:04:59,216
OH, HEY, JOEY.

121
00:04:59,216 --> 00:05:00,842
HEY.
WHAT'S UP?

122
00:05:00,842 --> 00:05:03,762
WELL, I CAN'T DECIDE
WHICH ROUTE TO TAKE TO VEGAS.

123
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:06,431
HEY... YOU'VE TRAVELED
A LOT, RIGHT?

124
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,308
YEAH, I'VE BEEN AROUND.
OKAY...

125
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,893
SO... SO WHICH ROUTE
SHOULD I TAKE

126
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:11,770
THE NORTHERN ROUTE
OR THE SOUTHERN ROUTE?

127
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:13,438
OOH, IF YOU TAKE
THE NORTHERN ROUTE

128
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,649
THERE'S A MAN IN ILLINOIS
WITH A BEARD OF BEES.

129
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:17,109
( gasps )

130
00:05:17,109 --> 00:05:20,279
GREAT! PROBLEM SOLVED.

131
00:05:20,279 --> 00:05:21,947
BUT ON THE SOUTHERN ROUTE

132
00:05:21,947 --> 00:05:24,491
THERE'S A CHICKEN THAT
PLAYS TIC-TAC-TOE.

133
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:28,036
WELL, BACK TO SQUARE ONE.

134
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:30,122
OH, I KNOW A WAY
THAT YOU CAN DECIDE.

135
00:05:30,122 --> 00:05:33,167
ALL RIGHT, I'M GOING TO ASK
YOU A SERIES OF QUESTIONS

136
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:35,294
AND YOU ANSWER AS
QUICKLY AS YOU CAN.

137
00:05:35,294 --> 00:05:36,628
( quickly ):
YES.

138
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:37,963
GOOD, BUT WAIT.

139
00:05:37,963 --> 00:05:40,007
OKAY... ALL RIGHT

140
00:05:40,007 --> 00:05:42,176
HERE WE GO. NOW, I
WANT YOU TO RELAX...

141
00:05:42,176 --> 00:05:45,470
TAKE A DEEP BREATH,
CLEAR YOUR MIND...

142
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,847
WHICH DO YOU
LIKE BETTER

143
00:05:46,847 --> 00:05:49,308
PEANUT BUTTER
OR EGG WHITES?
PEANUT BUTTER.

144
00:05:49,308 --> 00:05:51,685
WOULD YOU RATHER BE A
FIREMAN OR A SWIMMER?
A SWIMMER.

145
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:55,480
WOULD YOU RATHER SLEEP
WITH MONICA OR RACHEL?
MONICA. OH...

146
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,899
HUH. I ALWAYS THOUGHT
IT'D BE RACHEL.

147
00:05:57,899 --> 00:06:00,027
NO THINKING, NO THINKING.

148
00:06:00,027 --> 00:06:01,611
TIE OR ASCOT?
ASCOT.

149
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:03,280
NORTH ROUTE OR
SOUTH ROUTE?
NORTH ROUTE.

150
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,781
BAM! THERE YOU GO, HUH?

151
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:05,782
WOW.

152
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,534
THAT WAS INCREDIBLE.

153
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:09,744
BEARD OF BEES, HERE I COME.

154
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:12,539
HEY.

155
00:06:12,539 --> 00:06:15,416
OH, THIS GUY AGAIN.

156
00:06:17,044 --> 00:06:18,461
HEY, MAN,
WHAT'S UP?

157
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:19,796
UH, NOT MUCH.

158
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:21,798
YOU GUYS WANT TO SEE
A MOVIE TONIGHT?

159
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:23,382
SURE, WHAT DO YOU WANT TO SEE?

160
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:24,759
WELL, I DON'T KNOW. UM...

161
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:25,886
I KNOW HOW WE CAN DECIDE.

162
00:06:25,886 --> 00:06:27,054
PHOEBE, SHOW HIM YOUR GAME.

163
00:06:27,054 --> 00:06:28,347
UM, NO THANK YOU.

164
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,933
WHAT'S WITH HER?

165
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:33,060
I DON'T KNOW.

166
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,311
BUT, HEY, I KNOW
HOW WE CAN DECIDE.

167
00:06:34,311 --> 00:06:35,436
OKAY, I'M GOING
TO ASK YOU QUESTIONS

168
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:36,855
AND YOU ANSWER
REAL QUICK, OKAY?

169
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:37,981
OKAY.

170
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,816
ACTION OR COMEDY?
ACTION.

171
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:42,819
WHO WOULD YOU RATHER SLEEP WITH,
MONICA OR RACHEL?

172
00:06:47,032 --> 00:06:50,202
DUDE, YOU ARE SICK.

173
00:06:50,202 --> 00:06:53,538
OH, RIGHT, I'M SORRY.

174
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:54,622
I FORGOT YOU HAD
THAT WHOLE RACHEL THING.

175
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:55,582
I'M SORRY.

176
00:07:01,213 --> 00:07:02,214
OH, MY GOD.

177
00:07:02,214 --> 00:07:04,216
WHAT DOES THAT THING DO?

178
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:07,426
HMM, IT'S AN EYE
REMOVAL MACHINE.

179
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:08,762
ALL RIGHT, I'M OUT OF HERE.

180
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:09,930
I'M KIDDING, I'M KIDDING.

181
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:11,390
UH-OH.
HI, RACHEL.
HEY.

182
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,640
I'M DR. MILLER.

183
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,975
MONICA TOLD ME
YOU WERE A LITTLE NERVOUS

184
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:15,852
BUT EVERYTHING'S
GOING TO BE JUST FINE.

185
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:17,271
SO, WE'RE DONE THEN.

186
00:07:17,271 --> 00:07:19,231
ALMOST-- FIRST
WE GOT TO START.
OKAY.

187
00:07:19,231 --> 00:07:20,565
THIS IS THE GLAUCOMA TEST.

188
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:21,566
UH-HUH.

189
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:22,567
SIT DOWN.

190
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:23,902
OKAY.

191
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:26,071
PUT YOUR CHIN HERE.
MM-HMM.

192
00:07:26,071 --> 00:07:27,614
NOW, YOU'RE
GOING TO FEEL

193
00:07:27,614 --> 00:07:29,532
A SMALL PUFF OF
AIR IN EACH EYE.

194
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:31,618
W-WH-WHAT?

195
00:07:31,618 --> 00:07:32,911
A SMALL PUFF OF AIR.

196
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:34,537
( sharply ):
NOW, COME ON!

197
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:37,624
HERE WE GO.

198
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:38,625
ALL RIGHT.

199
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:40,877
ONE, TWO, THREE.

200
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:43,588
OKAY, I'M SORRY.

201
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:44,923
ALL RIGHT, JUST...

202
00:07:44,923 --> 00:07:47,008
I'M STAYING HERE THIS TIME.

203
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,009
OKAY.

204
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:49,303
READY?
UH-HUH.

205
00:07:49,303 --> 00:07:51,471
ONE, TWO, TH...

206
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:52,472
I'M SORRY.

207
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,681
YOU KNOW WHAT?

208
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:55,267
I'M GOING TO
HOLD HER HEAD.

209
00:07:55,267 --> 00:07:56,268
THAT'S OKAY.

210
00:07:56,268 --> 00:07:57,685
OKAY.
OKAY.

211
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:58,937
OKAY.

212
00:07:58,937 --> 00:08:00,605
ONE...
UH-HUH.

213
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,649
TWO...
I'M SORRY.

214
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:04,276
YOU KNOW WHAT?
YOU'RE YOUNG

215
00:08:04,276 --> 00:08:05,484
YOU PROBABLY DON'T
HAVE GLAUCOMA.

216
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:08,280
( cheering )

217
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,572
OKAY, SO...

218
00:08:09,572 --> 00:08:12,200
IT'S WAS VERY,
VERY NICE TO MEET YOU.

219
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:15,203
OH, HEY... WHAT, ARE YOU CRAZY?

220
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:17,122
OKAY, YOU HAVE A SMALL,
MINOR INFECTION

221
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:19,207
IN THAT LEFT EYE.

222
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,208
I WANT YOU TO
TAKE THESE DROPS

223
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,501
THREE TIMES A
DAY FOR A WEEK

224
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,086
AND YOU'LL BE
AS GOOD AS NEW.

225
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:25,505
NO, I DON'T PUT THINGS
IN MY EYE.

226
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,965
OKAY, THEN, I GUESS
WE'LL SEE YOU

227
00:08:26,965 --> 00:08:28,508
BACK HERE IN
THREE MONTHS.

228
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,469
GREAT.
AND I'LL FIT YOU
FOR A GLASS EYE.

229
00:08:30,469 --> 00:08:32,262
OKAY, JUST GIVE ME
THE DAMN DROPS.

230
00:08:34,139 --> 00:08:35,474
DR. MILLER...

231
00:08:35,474 --> 00:08:38,477
P-E-C-F-D.

232
00:08:38,477 --> 00:08:41,771
VERY GOOD, MONICA.

233
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:45,066
YOU KNOW WHERE THEY ARE.

234
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,276
I SURE DO.

235
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:51,490
AND YOU DON'T GET ONE.

236
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:58,205
YOU KNOW,
I GOT TO TELL YOU

237
00:08:58,205 --> 00:08:59,622
THOSE EYE DROPS
ARE A MIRACLE

238
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:01,666
MY EYE IS
100 PERCENT BETTER.

239
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:03,626
THEY'RE STILL IN MY COAT.

240
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:04,627
DAMN.

241
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:05,795
HEY.

242
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,047
HEY, YOU READY TO GO?

243
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:08,756
YEAH. HOW COLD IS IT
GOING TO BE?

244
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:11,134
DO I NEED A COAT OR WILL ALL
THESE SWEATER-VESTS BE ENOUGH.

245
00:09:12,302 --> 00:09:13,303
WHAT?

246
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:14,554
I LOVE YOU.

247
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:18,683
MAN, I WISH ROSS
WAS COMING WITH US, YOU KNOW.

248
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:19,851
I'M GOING TO MISS HIM.

249
00:09:19,851 --> 00:09:21,186
THANKS A LOT.

250
00:09:21,186 --> 00:09:22,937
I JUST GOT THAT JERK
OUT OF MY MIND.

251
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,647
HEY, SO WHERE ARE WE STAYING?

252
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,233
IS THE MOVIE PUTTING US UP

253
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,442
IN A BIG HOTEL SUITE?

254
00:09:27,442 --> 00:09:28,527
AH, NO,
NOT REALLY.

255
00:09:28,527 --> 00:09:29,903
IT'S AN INDEPENDENT FILM

256
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:31,405
SO WE DON'T HAVE
A REAL BIG BUDGET.

257
00:09:31,405 --> 00:09:33,114
I FIGURED I'D JUST STAY
IN YOUR ROOM.

258
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:35,242
I SEE, BUT ONCE YOU GET
YOUR FIRST PAYCHECK

259
00:09:35,242 --> 00:09:37,660
YOU'LL BE SPRINGING FOR A BIG
HOTEL SUITE, RIGHT?

260
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:38,745
I MEAN LEAD IN A MOVIE

261
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:40,247
THEY MUST BE
PAYING YOU A LOT.

262
00:09:40,247 --> 00:09:41,915
OH, YEAH, CHECK THIS OUT--

263
00:09:41,915 --> 00:09:44,209
FOR EVERY DOLLAR
SHUTTER SPEED MAKES

264
00:09:44,209 --> 00:09:46,920
ONE PENNY OF IT GOES
RIGHT IN JOEY'S POCKET.

265
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,255
SO YOU DON'T GET PAID

266
00:09:48,255 --> 00:09:50,090
UNLESS THE MOVIE
MAKES MONEY?

267
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:53,634
DID YOU NOT HEAR
THE PLOT OF THE MOVIE?

268
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:57,931
SHE'S BEEN DEAD
FOR TEN YEARS.

269
00:09:57,931 --> 00:09:59,015
I'M GOING TO BE
A MILLIONAIRE!

270
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:02,227
HEY.
HEY.

271
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,687
JUST WANTED TO SAY GOOD-BYE
TO YOU GUYS

272
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,523
AND TO SEE IF MAYBE YOU GUYS

273
00:10:06,523 --> 00:10:08,775
WILL PLACE A LITTLE BET
FOR ME, HUH?

274
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:10,193
20 BUCKS ON BLACK 15.

275
00:10:10,193 --> 00:10:11,945
YOU GOT IT.
ALL RIGHT.

276
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:14,114
ALL RIGHT, BYE-BYE NOW.

277
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:15,782
BYE, YOU GUYS.
BYE.

278
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:17,576
I'LL SAY GOOD-BYE
AT THE CAR.
OKAY.

279
00:10:17,576 --> 00:10:21,037
OH, ANYBODY WANT TO SAY
GOOD-BYE TO ME AT THE CAR?

280
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:23,081
OH, HONEY, I'LL SAY GOOD-BYE
TO YOU AT THE CAR

281
00:10:23,081 --> 00:10:25,292
IF YOU DON'T MIND THE PUS.

282
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:28,795
SEE YA.

283
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,130
NO, WAIT A MINUTE.

284
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:31,465
THE PUS IS GOOD.

285
00:10:31,465 --> 00:10:33,091
IT MEANS IT'S HEALING.

286
00:10:37,471 --> 00:10:40,807
HEY, PHEEBS,
WHATCHA READING?

287
00:10:40,807 --> 00:10:42,601
PHEEBS?

288
00:10:45,604 --> 00:10:47,897
HELLO.

289
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,983
PHOEBE?

290
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:53,487
PHEE... PHEE... PHOEBE.

291
00:10:53,487 --> 00:10:55,655
PHOEBE, COME ON.

292
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,616
OH, I'M SORRY, I
DIDN'T SEE YOU THERE.

293
00:10:59,951 --> 00:11:02,412
PHEEBS, ARE YOU MAD AT ME
OR SOMETHING?

294
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:03,538
'CAUSE IF YOU ARE

295
00:11:03,538 --> 00:11:05,624
PLEASE TELL ME
WHAT IT IS I DID.

296
00:11:05,624 --> 00:11:07,542
WELL, IF YOU DON'T KNOW,
I CAN'T HELP YOU.

297
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:08,668
WELL, I DON'T KNOW.

298
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:09,752
WELL, I CAN'T HELP YOU.

299
00:11:11,630 --> 00:11:13,965
OKAY, WELL, WHATEVER IT IS

300
00:11:13,965 --> 00:11:16,510
I AM VERY, VERY SORRY, OKAY?

301
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:18,928
APOLOGY ACCEPTED.

302
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:20,180
OKAY.

303
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,432
SO, WE'RE GOOD?

304
00:11:22,432 --> 00:11:23,517
UH-HUH.

305
00:11:23,517 --> 00:11:24,892
ALL RIGHT.

306
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:26,311
THANKS.

307
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,564
I'LL SEE YOU LATER, OKAY?

308
00:11:29,564 --> 00:11:30,815
BYE, FAT ASS.

309
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,526
ALL RIGHT.

310
00:11:32,526 --> 00:11:34,902
PHOEBE, NOW COME ON

311
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,446
WOULD YOU PLEASE TELL ME
WHAT IT IS

312
00:11:36,446 --> 00:11:37,696
THAT MADE YOU SO MAD AT ME.

313
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:39,032
I DON'T KNOW.

314
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:40,783
I DON'T REMEMBER.

315
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,827
WELL, IF YOU CAN'T REMEMBER

316
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:45,288
CAN'T WE JUST FORGET ABOUT THIS?

317
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:46,705
OH, NO, I AM MAD AT YOU

318
00:11:46,705 --> 00:11:48,041
I KNOW THAT MUCH.

319
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:50,418
BUT I AM SORRY
ABOUT THE FAT ASS THING

320
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:53,796
'CAUSE YOU ACTUALLY HAVE
A VERY SWEET LITTLE HEINIE.

321
00:12:01,513 --> 00:12:03,848
MAN, I'M GETTING
PRETTY TIRED.

322
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:06,434
YOU MIGHT HAVE
TO TAKE OVER SOON.

323
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:08,562
WE'VE BEEN DRIVING
FOR A HALF HOUR.

324
00:12:08,562 --> 00:12:11,022
AND YOU HAVEN'T LOOKED
AT THE ROAD ONCE.

325
00:12:11,022 --> 00:12:12,649
DON'T WORRY, IT'S OUT THERE.

326
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:16,944
MAYBE I JUST
NEED LUNCH.
YEAH.

327
00:12:16,944 --> 00:12:18,112
YOU WANT TO EAT?

328
00:12:18,112 --> 00:12:20,365
MY TREAT.

329
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:22,950
ISN'T THAT ROSS'S
MONEY?

330
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:26,120
YEAH, OKAY,
ROSS'S TREAT.

331
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,872
WHERE DO YOU
WANT TO EAT?

332
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:28,915
I DON'T KNOW.

333
00:12:28,915 --> 00:12:29,916
OH, HEY

334
00:12:29,916 --> 00:12:31,418
I KNOW HOW WE CAN DECIDE.

335
00:12:31,418 --> 00:12:33,378
I'M GOING TO ASK YOU
A BUNCH OF QUESTIONS

336
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:35,338
AND THEN YOU HAVE TO
ANSWER REAL FAST, OKAY?

337
00:12:35,338 --> 00:12:36,755
SO, CLEAR YOUR MIND.

338
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:38,592
CLEAR IT RIGHT OUT.
CLEAR IT OUT. CLEAR.

339
00:12:38,592 --> 00:12:39,926
OKAY.

340
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:42,929
OKAY, WOULD YOU RATHER
BE TOO WET OR TOO DRY?

341
00:12:42,929 --> 00:12:44,723
TOO DRY.
DO YOU BELIEVE IN GHOSTS?

342
00:12:44,723 --> 00:12:47,058
NO.
IS THE MOVIE MY BIG BREAK?

343
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:48,976
NO.

344
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:50,186
WHAT?

345
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:51,896
YES.

346
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:52,897
DUDE, YOU SAID NO.

347
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,982
WELL, I ALSO
SAID YES.

348
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:57,444
WELL, YOU DON'T THINK
THIS IS GOING TO BE
A BIG BREAK FOR ME?

349
00:12:57,444 --> 00:13:01,114
NO...
( choking )

350
00:13:01,114 --> 00:13:02,490
I DON'T BELIEVE THIS.

351
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:04,492
LOOK, JOE, I JUST...

352
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:06,785
I JUST DON'T WANT YOU
TO GET YOUR HOPES UP
TOO HIGH, YOU KNOW?

353
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:08,455
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

354
00:13:08,455 --> 00:13:09,997
I'M THE LEAD IN A MOVIE.

355
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:12,584
THEY'RE NOT EVEN PAYING YOU.

356
00:13:12,584 --> 00:13:14,335
THIS DOESN'T EVEN SOUND
LIKE A REAL MOVIE.

357
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:16,003
I DON'T NEED THIS.

358
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:17,880
I DON'T KNOW WHY YOU'RE DUMPING
ON MY BIG BREAK.

359
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,592
'CAUSE, JOE, I DON'T THINK THIS
IS GOING TO BE YOUR BIG BREAK.

360
00:13:20,592 --> 00:13:22,051
IS THAT WHY YOU'RE
ON THIS TRIP, HUH?

361
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,595
TO MAKE ME FEEL
LIKE A LOSER?

362
00:13:23,595 --> 00:13:25,430
'CAUSE IF IT IS,
I'D RATHER BE ALONE.

363
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:26,847
YOU DON'T WANT ME HERE?

364
00:13:26,847 --> 00:13:28,308
NOT IF YOU'RE GOING
TO BE LIKE THIS.

365
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,143
TELL YOU WHAT--
THE NEXT TIME YOU ASK ME

366
00:13:30,143 --> 00:13:31,519
A QUESTION LIKE THAT,
I'LL LIE.

367
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:33,020
YEAH, I DON'T WANT YOU
ON THE TRIP.

368
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:34,897
ALL RIGHT, FINE, FINE.

369
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:39,860
WHY DON'T YOU PULL OVER,
I'LL GET OUT RIGHT NOW.
FINE.

370
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,446
GET OUT.

371
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,490
YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED
TO STOP ON A BRIDGE.

372
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:44,491
GET OUT!

373
00:13:44,491 --> 00:13:45,533
ALL RIGHT!

374
00:13:48,286 --> 00:13:50,997
Chandler:
WAIT! WAIT!
THERE'S NO SIDEWALK!

375
00:13:50,997 --> 00:13:52,624
YEAH, I'M GONNA DIE HERE.

376
00:13:56,835 --> 00:13:59,130
ARE YOU MAD AT ME
BECAUSE MY HAIR GEL SMELLS?

377
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:00,465
Phoebe:
NO.

378
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:02,550
ARE YOU ANGRY WITH ME
BECAUSE I SAID

379
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:05,011
YOUR HANDWRITING
IS CHILDLIKE?

380
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:07,221
NO, THAT MADE ME FEEL PRECIOUS.

381
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:09,098
OH, I KNOW.

382
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:11,976
UM, IS IT BECAUSE HE'S ALWAYS
CORRECTING PEOPLE'S GRAMMAR?

383
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:13,060
"WHOM, WHOM."

384
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,813
SOMETIMES IT'S "WHO."

385
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,231
YEAH, SOMETIMES IT'S...

386
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,903
OH, DID YOU BEAT HIM
AT A BOARD GAME?

387
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:25,365
HE TURNS INTO
SUCH A BABY WHEN
HE STARTS TO LOSE.

388
00:14:25,365 --> 00:14:29,285
OH, YEAH, I'M THE BABY.
HEY, STOP IT!

389
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:30,620
HEY.

390
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:32,246
CHANDLER, WHAT
ARE YOU DOING HERE?

391
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:33,623
JOEY KICKED ME OUT
OF THE CAR

392
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,166
ON THE GEORGE WASHINGTON
BRIDGE.

393
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:36,167
All:
WHY?

394
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:37,627
HE WENT CRAZY.

395
00:14:37,627 --> 00:14:39,671
WE WERE PLAYING THAT GAME
WHERE YOU ASK A QUESTION

396
00:14:39,671 --> 00:14:41,381
AND YOU HAVE
TO ANSWER REALLY FAST.

397
00:14:41,381 --> 00:14:44,801
OH, THAT GAME SHOULD NOT BE
PLAYED WITHOUT MY SUPERVISION.

398
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:47,721
WELL, I DON'T KNOW WHAT
MADE HIM SO MAD.

399
00:14:47,721 --> 00:14:49,389
ALL I SAID WAS THAT
I DIDN'T THINK

400
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:51,140
THIS WAS GOING TO BE
HIS BIG BREAK.

401
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:53,727
THAT THIS MOVIE WASN'T
GOING TO DO ANYTHING FOR HIM

402
00:14:53,727 --> 00:14:55,895
AND THAT IT DIDN'T SOUND
LIKE A REAL MOVIE.

403
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:58,231
OKAY, HE SHOULD HAVE
PUSHED ME OFF THE BRIDGE.

404
00:14:58,231 --> 00:14:59,566
WHAT'S IN THE BAG?

405
00:14:59,566 --> 00:15:01,651
OH, I FIGURED YOU GUYS
WOULD ALL BE MAD AT ME

406
00:15:01,651 --> 00:15:04,654
SO I GOT YOU SOME GIFTS
THAT I FOUND ON THE
SIDE OF THE ROAD.

407
00:15:04,654 --> 00:15:06,489
WHO WANTS THE TEDDY BEAR
WITH ONE LEG?

408
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:07,490
I DO.

409
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:12,953
OKAY...

410
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:18,125
NOT EVEN CLOSE.

411
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:19,586
OKAY, THEN HELP ME.
I NEED HELP.

412
00:15:19,586 --> 00:15:20,795
I CAN'T DO THIS.

413
00:15:20,795 --> 00:15:22,088
OKAY, COME ON,
LET'S DO IT.

414
00:15:22,088 --> 00:15:23,089
ALL RIGHT.

415
00:15:23,089 --> 00:15:24,215
SIT DOWN.

416
00:15:24,215 --> 00:15:25,550
ALL RIGHT, PUT
YOUR HEAD BACK.

417
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:27,343
YES.

418
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,887
ALL RIGHT,
NOW OPEN YOUR EYES.

419
00:15:28,887 --> 00:15:30,680
OKAY, THEY ARE.

420
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:33,933
HOW MANY FINGERS
AM I HOLDING UP?

421
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,184
FOUR.

422
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:36,644
OH, MY GOD, I WAS
THINKING FOUR.

423
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:37,645
REALLY?

424
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,397
YES!

425
00:15:39,397 --> 00:15:42,066
YOU KNOW WHAT? WHY DON'T WE
START WITH A PRACTICE ONE, OKAY?

426
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:43,067
NO DROPS.

427
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:44,444
GREAT.

428
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:46,863
OKAY, ALL RIGHT,
ON THREE.

429
00:15:46,863 --> 00:15:48,823
ONE... TWO... THREE.

430
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:51,992
MY PILLOW'S ALL WET.

431
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:54,161
WELL, YOU SAID IT WAS PRACTICE.

432
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:55,455
THEN WHY DID YOU MOVE?

433
00:15:55,455 --> 00:15:58,207
BECAUSE I KNEW YOU WERE LYING.

434
00:15:58,207 --> 00:15:59,250
ALL RIGHT, COME HERE.

435
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:00,668
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

436
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:02,002
GET... JUST GET...

437
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,170
MONICA, STOP IT!

438
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:04,547
OH, MY GOD!
STOP IT!

439
00:16:04,547 --> 00:16:05,548
I AM GOING...

440
00:16:05,548 --> 00:16:06,549
TURN IT OVER!

441
00:16:06,549 --> 00:16:08,092
NO!

442
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:09,844
I AM... I AM GOING
TO GET...

443
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:13,055
GET THESE DROPS
IN YOUR EYES.

444
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:14,223
OH, MY GOD!

445
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:16,517
YOU REALLY ARE
FREAKISHLY STRONG.

446
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:18,311
( screaming )

447
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:21,147
MONICA, STOP IT!

448
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:22,482
( coughs )

449
00:16:22,482 --> 00:16:24,108
DAMN, IT'S EMPTY!

450
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:26,945
WELL, IF JOEY AND CHANDLER
WALKED IN RIGHT NOW

451
00:16:26,945 --> 00:16:28,446
WE COULD MAKE A FORTUNE.

452
00:16:33,576 --> 00:16:35,077
( phone ringing )

453
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:37,413
OH, THAT IS DEFINITELY
CHANDLER, JOEY OR ROSS...

454
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:38,957
OR RACHEL.

455
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:42,627
HELLO.

456
00:16:42,627 --> 00:16:43,878
IT'S JOEY.

457
00:16:44,963 --> 00:16:46,380
I'M SO GLAD
YOU CALLED.

458
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:47,924
CHANDLER TOLD ME WHAT HAPPENED.

459
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:49,801
YOU KNOW, HE'S REALLY
UPSET ABOUT IT.

460
00:16:49,801 --> 00:16:53,429
NOT AS UPSET AS HE'S GOING TO BE
WHEN HE FINDS OUT WHAT I DID

461
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:54,764
WITH HIS SWEATER-VESTS.

462
00:16:56,182 --> 00:16:58,309
WHAT DID YOU DO
TO HIS SWEATER-VESTS?

463
00:16:58,309 --> 00:17:01,145
LET'S JUST SAY THERE'S
A WELL-DRESSED PACK OF DOGS
IN OHIO.

464
00:17:03,731 --> 00:17:05,608
Hey, Monica, is Phoebe there?

465
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:07,067
I'VE GOT TO ASK HER SOMETHING
ABOUT THE CAR.

466
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:09,111
Yeah, she's here.
Hold on one second.

467
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:10,363
HEY, DUDE.

468
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:11,906
Hey, Pheebs.

469
00:17:11,906 --> 00:17:14,032
THIS BOX KEEPS SLIDING OUT
FROM UNDER THE SEAT.

470
00:17:14,032 --> 00:17:15,117
WHAT IS IT?

471
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:16,160
OH, THAT'S MY GRANDMA.

472
00:17:19,330 --> 00:17:20,665
AND THANKS, JOEY.

473
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:22,542
SHE'S HAVING
A REALLY GREAT TIME.

474
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:26,170
IS THAT JOEY?
IS THAT JOEY?

475
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,755
LET ME TALK TO HIM.

476
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,131
OKAY, JOEY, CHANDLER'S HERE.
HE WAS WONDERING IF...

477
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:30,758
( line disconnects )

478
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:32,719
OKAY, I GUESS HE RAN OUT
OF CHANGE.

479
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,596
YOU KNOW, HE WON'T
EVEN TALK TO ME.

480
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:37,097
HOW AM I GOING
TO APOLOGIZE TO HIM

481
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:38,307
IF HE WON'T EVEN
TALK TO ME?

482
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:40,267
MAYBE YOU SHOULD
SEND HIM SOMETHING.

483
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:42,478
SO WHEN HE GETS TO LAS VEGAS
HE'LL KNOW THAT YOU'RE SORRY.

484
00:17:42,478 --> 00:17:44,772
THAT'S A GOOD IDEA.

485
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:47,775
I WONDER WHERE I COULD
GET A BASKET OF PORN?

486
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:50,862
OH, NO, NO, DON'T SAY I'M SORRY
WITH PORN.

487
00:17:50,862 --> 00:17:52,071
NO?

488
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:53,155
YOU KNOW WHAT
YOU SHOULD SEND HIM--

489
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:55,491
A CARTON OF CIGARETTES.

490
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,159
'CAUSE THAT WAY HE CAN TRADE IT
FOR PROTECTION...

491
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:59,453
NO, THAT'S PRISON.

492
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:01,288
( door opening )

493
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:05,251
OKAY, PHEEBS, I KNOW HOW
WE'RE GOING TO FIGURE THIS OUT.

494
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:06,878
OKAY, CLEAR YOUR MIND

495
00:18:06,878 --> 00:18:10,924
AND ANSWER THE FIRST THING
THAT COMES INTO YOUR HEAD, OKAY?

496
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:12,341
MM-HMM.

497
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:14,092
WHAT DO YOU LIKE BETTER,
FLORA OR FAUNA?

498
00:18:14,092 --> 00:18:16,178
FAUNA.
SIMON OR GARFUNKLE?

499
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,513
GARFUNKLE.
WHY ARE YOU MAD AT ME?

500
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:19,306
YOU SAID I WAS BORING. OH!

501
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:23,811
WHEN DID I SAY
YOU WERE BORING?

502
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,605
OH, MY GOD! I REMEMBER NOW!

503
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:27,147
WE WERE PLAYING CHESS.

504
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:30,276
PHOEBE, YOU AND I HAVE
NEVER PLAYED CHESS.

505
00:18:30,276 --> 00:18:31,611
OH, COME ON, YES.

506
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:33,153
REMEMBER THAT TIME
ON THE FROZEN LAKE

507
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:34,280
WE WERE PLAYING CHESS.

508
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,074
YOU SAID I WAS BORING

509
00:18:36,074 --> 00:18:37,283
AND THEN YOU TOOK OFF
YOUR ENERGY MASK

510
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:39,702
AND YOU WERE CAMERON DIAZ.

511
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:45,291
OKAY, THERE'S A CHANCE
THIS MAY HAVE BEEN A DREAM.

512
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:14,236
HEY.

513
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:15,488
STANLEY!

514
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:17,073
HEY-HEY!

515
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:18,992
YOUR LEADING MAN IS HERE.
LET'S GET TO WORK.

516
00:19:18,992 --> 00:19:21,744
UM, SLIGHT
CHANGE OF PLANS.

517
00:19:21,744 --> 00:19:23,370
WE'VE SHUT DOWN.

518
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:24,622
WHA... WHAT?

519
00:19:24,622 --> 00:19:25,623
WHY?

520
00:19:25,623 --> 00:19:27,000
IT'S A MONEY THING.

521
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,250
WE DON'T HAVE ANY.

522
00:19:29,669 --> 00:19:31,004
( chuckling )

523
00:19:31,004 --> 00:19:33,047
YOU'RE KIDDING, RIGHT?
NO.

524
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:34,381
WHAT?

525
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:36,134
IT'S PROBABLY
JUST TEMPORARY.

526
00:19:36,134 --> 00:19:38,636
WE'RE HOPING TO GET
SOME MORE MONEY SOON.

527
00:19:38,636 --> 00:19:40,513
SO IF YOU COULD
JUST HANG OUT.

528
00:19:40,513 --> 00:19:41,848
HANG OUT?

529
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:43,182
HOW LONG?

530
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,143
I DON'T KNOW,
A WEEK, MAYBE TWO.

531
00:19:45,143 --> 00:19:46,560
THE MONEY WILL
TURN UP.

532
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,646
PEOPLE ALWAYS WANT
TO INVEST IN MOVIES.

533
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:50,272
HEY, YOU'RE NOT RICH, ARE YOU?

534
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,108
NO.
WORTH A SHOT.

535
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:57,279
LOOK, JOEY, LET ME KNOW
WHERE YOU'RE STAYING, OKAY?

536
00:19:58,865 --> 00:20:00,616
HEY, PAL.

537
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:02,451
ARE YOU JOEY TRIBBIANI?
YEAH.

538
00:20:02,451 --> 00:20:05,287
THESE GOT
LEFT FOR YOU.
THANKS.

539
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:10,043
"CONGRATULATIONS
ON YOUR BIG BREAK."

540
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:42,116
( phone ringing )

541
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:43,409
HELLO.

542
00:20:43,409 --> 00:20:44,827
Hey, Monica, it's Joey.

543
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:46,453
HEY, JOEY.

544
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:48,414
OH, YOU REMEMBER ME EVEN THOUGH
YOU'RE A BIG STAR.

545
00:20:48,414 --> 00:20:49,749
Oh, come on.

546
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:51,625
It'll be years
before I forget you.

547
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:55,546
JOEY, WHAT'S IT LIKE
ON A MOVIE SET, HUH?

548
00:20:55,546 --> 00:20:57,255
DO YOU HAVE A DRESSING ROOM?

549
00:20:57,255 --> 00:20:58,758
DO YOU HAVE A CHAIR
WITH YOUR NAME ON IT?

550
00:20:58,758 --> 00:21:00,927
Yeah, yeah, I got all that
going on, yeah.

551
00:21:00,927 --> 00:21:03,470
Listen, I want you to make sure
you tell Chandler

552
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:05,472
that he couldn't have
been more wrong.

553
00:21:05,472 --> 00:21:07,265
Uh-oh, I got to go, Monica.

554
00:21:07,265 --> 00:21:08,684
My... my sushi's here.

555
00:21:12,438 --> 00:21:13,731
SORRY ABOUT THAT.

556
00:21:13,731 --> 00:21:15,191
THANKS FOR WAITING.

557
00:21:15,191 --> 00:21:16,192
OKAY.

558
00:21:16,192 --> 00:21:17,860
EVERYBODY SMILE.

559
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:19,862
OKAY.

560
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:20,905
THANKS A LOT.

561
00:21:20,905 --> 00:21:22,573
ENJOY YOUR STAY AT CAESARS.

562
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:25,283
WE HOPE IT'S TOGA-RIFFIC.

563
00:21:27,285 --> 00:21:29,122
KILL ME. KILL ME NOW.

564
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,879
RACHE, CAN YOU PASS
ME THE TV GUIDE?

565
00:21:36,879 --> 00:21:38,089
YEAH.

566
00:21:38,089 --> 00:21:39,090
GO!

567
00:21:39,090 --> 00:21:40,091
WHAT?!

568
00:21:40,091 --> 00:21:41,467
GET AWAY!

569
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:43,385
OH, MY GOD!

570
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:45,554
Monica:
HOLD HER. OKAY.

571
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,437
WE'LL SEE YOU IN ABOUT
THREE OR FOUR HOURS.

572
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:55,481
AW.

